# Text is stored with LF endings.
# Batch files keep CRLF, because cmd.exe can misread labels in a file with LF endings.
# Flight files keep the sim's own bytes, CRLF and Windows-1252, because the sim reads
# them back and we haven't tested whether it accepts any other form.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.[fF][lL][tT] -text
